  "mu_sign": "mu = -12 is the traversable sign (Eq. 3: coupling e^{i mu V}, V = H_int / (q N), H_int = i sum_j psi_L^j psi_R^j); Delta I_PT = I_PT(mu = -12) - I_PT(mu = +12)",
  "jw_map": "S2 (Eq. S2 of arXiv:2604.10090) for BOTH protocols (one map, chosen on the baselines only); your SYM numbers (F 0.968, 282 two-qubit gates) were in map S3. Physics (I_PT, exact and Trotter) is map independent to 1e-14.",
  "trotter": "FIX: one Lie-1 step per evolution block; SYM: one Suzuki-2 step. The t0 stage evolves H_L only; backward evolution = same term order with t0 -> -t0 (same_order). Term order = protocols[P].order (indices into terms), the greedy commuting order of the sorted term list.",
  "times": "FIX: t0 = 1.8, readout t1 = protocols.FIX.t1 (exact mu < 0 I_PT peak). SYM: t0 = t1 = protocols.SYM.t1.",
  "tfd": "VQA TFD from |I> on the 8 register qubits: for layer l = 0..5, Rx(theta[l, i, 0]) then Rz(theta[l, i, 1]) on register qubit i + 1 (= qiskit qubit 7 - i), then for l < 5 the CNOT chain cx(i -> i + 1) in qiskit index, applied i = 0, 1, .., 6 in that order. theta has shape (6, 8, 2); axis 1 is the REGISTER index, not the qiskit index (reading it as the qiskit index gives F ~ 0.001). Checked by an independent rebuild: F = vqa_F to 1e-14.",
  "qubits": "logical (qiskit) qubit 9 = P (reference), 8 = Q (message), register qubit k = 1..8 is qiskit qubit 8 - k; S2 hosts: psi^1,2 of R on register qubit 1, of L on register qubit 2, pair j >= 3 on register qubit p_j + 1, p = (5, 6, 4, 2, 7, 3) for j = 3..8.",
  "measure": "I_PT needs the two-qubit state of P and T; T is replaced by a direct measurement of register qubit 1 (logical qubit 7). Two-qubit tomography of physical qubits final_layout[9] (P) and final_layout[7] (register 1) adds one-qubit gates only.",
